    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d608-a1">

                <pb facs="0709" n="613" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg613"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Marquis of Salisbury to Sir Julian
                        Pauncefote.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-03-04"><hi rendition="#italic">March 4,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Article 5, Section V, of general act for government of Samoan Islands.</p>
                <p>German Government suggest that, in the event of any doubt arising as to the
                    competency of the provisional (?) government of Samoa under this section, the
                    new president should, as a preliminary arrangement, be appointed by the consuls
                    of the powers without the cooperation of the Samoan authorities.</p>
                <p>Please ascertain if the United States Government concur.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
